            <ArticleTitle>Is magnesium sulfate friend or foe of off-pump coronary artery bypass surgery?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>258-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ihj.2015.09.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0019-4832(15)00398-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Magnesium sulfate is often used empirically in cardiac surgical settings. Magnesium sulfate may cause platelet dysfunction leading to bleeding complication. This editorial commentary discusses the published study of intra-operative use of magnesium sulfate during off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting published in this issue of Indian Heart Journal.</AbstractText>
